.TH PKCSCONF 1 "August 2026" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "openCryptoki"
.SH NAME
pkcsconf \- configuration utility for the pkcsslotd daemon

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpkcsconf\fP
[\fB-itsmlIupPh\fP]
[\fB-c\fP \fIslotnumber\fP]
[\fB-U\fP \fIuserPIN\fP]
[\fB-S\fP \fISOPIN\fP]
[\fB-n\fP \fInewpin\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpkcsconf\fP utility displays and configures the state of the
pkcsslotd daemon and the tokens managed by the daemon.

.SH "COMMAND SUMMARY"
.IP "\fB-i\fP" 10
display PKCS11 info
.IP "\fB-t\fP" 10
display token info
.IP "\fB-s\fP" 10
display slot info
.IP "\fB-m\fP" 10
display mechanism list
.IP "\fB-l\fP" 10
display slot description
.IP "\fB-I\fP" 10
initialize token; requires \fB-c\fP.
The SO PIN must be supplied via \fB-S\fP or will be prompted for.
.IP "\fB-u\fP" 10
initialize user PIN; requires \fB-c\fP.
The SO PIN must be supplied via \fB-S\fP or will be prompted for.
The new user PIN must be supplied via \fB-n\fP or will be prompted for.
.IP "\fB-p\fP" 10
set the user PIN; requires \fB-c\fP.
The current user PIN must be supplied via \fB-U\fP or will be prompted for.
The new user PIN must be supplied via \fB-n\fP or will be prompted for.
Mutually exclusive with \fB-P\fP.
.IP "\fB-P\fP" 10
set the SO PIN; requires \fB-c\fP.
The current SO PIN must be supplied via \fB-S\fP or will be prompted for.
The new SO PIN must be supplied via \fB-n\fP or will be prompted for.
Mutually exclusive with \fB-p\fP.
.IP "\fB-c\fP \fISLOT\fP" 10
specify the token slot for the operation;
required when using \fB-I\fP, \fB-u\fP, \fB-p\fP, or \fB-P\fP
.IP "\fB-U\fP \fIUSERPIN\fP" 10
the current user PIN (for use when changing the user PIN; \fB-p\fP option);
if not specified, user will be prompted
.IP "\fB-S\fP \fISOPIN\fP" 10
the current Security Officer (SO) PIN (for use when initializing the token or
user PIN, or changing the SO PIN; \fB-I\fP, \fB-u\fP, and \fB-P\fP options);
if not specified, user will be prompted
.IP "\fB-n\fP \fINEWPIN\fP" 10
the new PIN (for use when initializing the user PIN or changing the user or SO
PIN; \fB-u\fP, \fB-p\fP, and \fB-P\fP options); if not specified, user will be
prompted
.IP "\fB-h\fP" 10
show usage information

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B >0
A PKCS#11 error code is returned on failure.

.SH SEE ALSO
.PD 0
.TP
\fBopencryptoki\fP(7),
.TP
\fBpkcsslotd\fP(8).
.PD
